00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.180
When working with documents, it
is important that the content

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:04.470
is structured effectively.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.440
Windows has a number of tools
that allow you to do this.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:10.740
And what we're going to be looking
at in this video is the tools that

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.030
you can find on the layout tab.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.230
So if we clicked on the layout tab,
as you can see, there are three

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:20.040
sections here, and we're primarily
going to focus on the first two, which

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:26.820
is margins, page orientations, size,
columns, breaks and the way you can

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.640
indent and space the paragraphs around.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:34.970
One of the tools that we're going to
look at first is the widows and orphans.

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:37.250
As you can see, it's unticked here.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.160
By default, this will be
ticked in your Windows program.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:49.090
If the widows and orphans box isn't
ticked, as you can see, when I start

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:52.580
pressing the enter key and moving
text further down the table and I

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:57.920
move onto a new page it actually
allows the splitting up of paragraphs.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:03.050
So you can have information
starting on one line and not

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:04.430
finishing till the next line.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:14.170
So if I just undo what I've done
there, and then I select the widows

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:17.470
and orphan control, make sure
that's ticked and select okay.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:23.210
And then, press the enter key again, to
take the information onto the next page,

00:01:26.170 --> 00:01:28.240
you will see that it jumps the paragraph.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:33.160
It won't let you have just
one line on the previous page.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.140
Just undo that.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:44.440
Another feature that you may find
useful is the ability to keep paragraphs

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.330
together or lines in a paragraph together.

00:01:46.835 --> 00:01:50.345
If you click on the paragraph
expansion control there, as you

00:01:50.345 --> 00:01:53.555
can see, I've got keep lines
together ticked in that box there.

00:01:55.625 --> 00:01:59.705
What this means is that when I press the
enter key and move text further down the

00:01:59.705 --> 00:02:05.855
table, when it moves on to a new page,
it automatically moves a whole paragraph.

00:02:05.975 --> 00:02:08.105
So it won't let you split a paragraph up.

00:02:14.365 --> 00:02:15.535
I'll just move that back.

00:02:16.595 --> 00:02:19.555
The next tool I'm going to
look at is the page break tool.

00:02:20.675 --> 00:02:24.245
As you can see, all the information is
on one page there, but there is a blank

00:02:24.275 --> 00:02:28.805
second page, but just back space that
and that everything is on one page.

00:02:29.345 --> 00:02:33.425
So for example, I wish to
move the information from this

00:02:33.425 --> 00:02:35.615
point forward onto a new page.

00:02:36.095 --> 00:02:39.335
I can go to breaks and
select a page break.

00:02:39.575 --> 00:02:42.455
Now that automatically moves
the information on to page two.

00:02:44.615 --> 00:02:45.555
Now, that's fine.

00:02:45.575 --> 00:02:50.015
But say, for example, I wanted to
have this page in landscape format

00:02:50.045 --> 00:02:52.024
and keep this page in portrait format.

00:02:52.954 --> 00:02:56.614
If I tried that now, so the cursor is
blinking, I've changed the orientation to

00:02:56.614 --> 00:02:59.975
landscape, both pages change to landscape.

00:03:00.274 --> 00:03:01.714
So I will just undo that.

00:03:03.575 --> 00:03:08.705
What I need to do here is I need to undo
the page break that was inserted and

00:03:08.765 --> 00:03:13.535
rather than insert a page break, I need
to insert a section break next page.

00:03:14.375 --> 00:03:18.385
What this does it again, moves
the information on the page two

00:03:19.305 --> 00:03:22.595
but, this allows me to format
this page in any way I want.

00:03:22.655 --> 00:03:26.465
So I can now select the
orientation and landscape, and

00:03:26.465 --> 00:03:28.235
it will only change that page.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.220
As you can see if I go to the
home tab and use the show and hide

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:35.930
button to see the formatting that
is being applied, as you can see

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.640
there is a section break next page.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.460
So that has basically moved
everything down and the

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:42.260
formatting that's applied to that.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:45.290
The layout of that page can
be different to page one.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:58.745
If I remove the show and hide, click
off that and then insert another section

00:03:58.745 --> 00:04:02.465
break next page from the layout tab.

00:04:04.535 --> 00:04:06.605
This third page can then be changed again.

00:04:06.815 --> 00:04:09.245
So for example, I could go
back to portrait for that one.

00:04:09.245 --> 00:04:13.925
So as you can see, I can have
one page in portrait, one page in

00:04:13.925 --> 00:04:18.485
landscape, and then when I wish to
continue with the document, I can

00:04:18.515 --> 00:04:21.935
have the third page back in portrait.

00:04:22.805 --> 00:04:26.705
Another tool that you may find useful
is that you may present information in

00:04:26.705 --> 00:04:30.815
column format, so rather than having
the text spread all across the page,

00:04:31.175 --> 00:04:34.385
you may have a document where you
need to insert it in column format.

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:38.044
So if I place the cursor at the
front of the text on the first page.

00:04:38.495 --> 00:04:41.435
And if I look at the columns
button, I click on that, I can

00:04:41.435 --> 00:04:44.255
change it to 1, 2, 3 columns.

00:04:44.555 --> 00:04:46.805
So just as an example, I'll
change that to two columns.

00:04:47.495 --> 00:04:50.450
As you can see all of the text
has now been bunched up on the

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:51.520
left-hand side of the page.

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:56.450
If I just insert the cursor there
and press the enter key, as you can

00:04:56.450 --> 00:05:01.760
see, it is now moving the text to
another column on the same page.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.900
This can be useful if you're presenting
something such as a newsletter.

00:05:09.469 --> 00:05:13.045
As your document increases in size
it would be useful to insert page

00:05:13.045 --> 00:05:19.825
numbers so you can identify the pages
as the document grows to do this,

00:05:19.825 --> 00:05:22.225
we need to go to the insert tab.

00:05:22.285 --> 00:05:26.125
So I click on insert and as you
can see if I look along to the

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:29.935
header and footer section, there's
the option to insert page numbers.

00:05:30.710 --> 00:05:34.070
So I can click on the page number and
it will ask me if I wish to place it

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:38.099
at the top of the page, to the bottom
of the page and the margin of the page.

00:05:38.539 --> 00:05:40.520
For this one, I'm just going to
select the bottom of the page.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:45.520
As you can see the variety of
formatting that can be applied to

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:47.030
the way the page number is entered.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:51.669
For this one, I'm going to simply
select plain number two, and that

00:05:51.669 --> 00:05:55.030
will insert a page number in the
footer section of the document.

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:56.440
So just click away from that.

00:05:56.860 --> 00:06:00.919
And as you can see, that has
automatically inserted page numbers on

00:06:00.919 --> 00:06:03.049
the three pages within this document.

